---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Authority is recognised" currentPath="/manifesto/foundations/authority">
  <div class="breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Entry</a> / <a href="/manifesto">Manifesto</a> / <a href="/manifesto/foundations">Foundations</a> / Authority
  </div>

  <article class="principle-document">
    <header class="principle-header">
      <div class="principle-meta">
        <span class="principle-number">I.2</span>
        <span class="plate-id">E01-P02</span>
      </div>
      <h1>Authority is recognised</h1>
      <p class="abstract">Authority emerges through coherence held over time, not assertion or display.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="principle-content">
      <h2>Statement</h2>
      <p>Authority is not claimed.</p>
      <p>It is recognised when a system no longer needs to explain itself.</p>

      <h2>Context</h2>
      <p>
        Systems that assert authority undermine it. True authority accumulates through consistent behavior—through maintaining coherence even when pressure exists to deviate.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is why promotional language weakens credibility. The system that must convince you of its value demonstrates uncertainty about that value.
      </p>

      <h2>Application</h2>
      <p>
        Authority manifests through predictability. Users learn they can depend on the system to behave consistently. This dependability becomes the foundation of trust, which is how authority is actually conferred.
      </p>

      <h2>Citation</h2>
      <p class="citation-text">
        This principle may be cited as: <strong>I.2 (Authority)</strong> or by plate reference <strong>E01-P02</strong>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .breadcrumb {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .breadcrumb a:hover {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .principle-document {
    max-width: 700px;
  }

  .principle-header {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .principle-meta {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .principle-header h1 {
    font-size: 2.25rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .abstract {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .principle-content h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .principle-content p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .citation-text {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .citation-text strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-style: normal;
  }
</style>
